<title>JAPAN: Japan, US setting up port talks in Washington Mar 3.</title>
<headline>Japan, US setting up port talks in Washington Mar 3.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. and Japanese officials are working to set up talks on Japan's controversial port practices on March 3 in Washington, a transport ministry official said on Friday.</p>
<p>The talks would follow Wednesday's decision by the U.S. Federal Maritime Commission (FMC) to impose $100,000 surcharges on Japanese vessels calling at U.S. ports in retaliation for what it called &quot;unfavourable restrictive practices&quot;.</p>
<p>The surcharges would go into effect on April 14.  </p>
<p>The official said Masazumi Nagamitsu, deputy director of the Transport Ministry's Maritime Transport Bureau, would take part in the talks along with foreign ministry officials.</p>
<p>But he declined to comment on prospects for resolving the dispute.</p>
</text>
